[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;/a&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;br&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Helvetica Neue&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,248][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    Malicious actors can track Android, Windows, or Linux devices through an Apple Find My network vulnerability using malware that mimics AirTag signals. They can monitor movements remotely, affecting smartphones, computers, smart TVs, etc. Apple has issued patches, and users should disable Bluetooth when not in use and keep devices updated.[\n]"
