[2025-04-14 21:29:24,256][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                    The NSO Group&apos;s BLASTPASS exploit targets iPhones via iMessage through a WebP vulnerability. The attack involves sending a PKPass file with a WebP image that caused a buffer overflow, overwriting a pointer, and executing malicious code via heap manipulation that bypasses iOS protections like ASLR and PAC. Unlike earlier exploits that need complex &quot;weird machines,&quot; BLASTPASS uses conventional techniques such as callback-oriented programming and a multi-stage approach, with follow-up iMessages delivering final payload encryption keys.[\n]"
[2025-04-14 21:29:24,256][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-18 << "                                &lt;/span&gt;[\n]"
