[2025-04-14 21:29:26,329][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-20 << ";noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Jason Kao&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; discusses how to effectively combine Resource Control Policies (RCPs) and Service Control Policies (SCPs), including an example of how to migrate from an SCP to RCP. Recommendations: Use RCPs when you[0xe2][0x80][0x99]re protecting resources in S3, STS, KMS, SQS, or Secrets Manager, are enforcing consistent security standards for resources, are running out of attachment room or space in SCPs, or you want to use NotResource in your policy. Use SCPs if you need to restrict a service not covered by RCPs or you want to use NotAction.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565Shz-FkwPqTW6hJuIjzacjKzHa4CNJ_g8sJAnX9ZRlK-lphCKR-oT677wJ_h8WMHJjnWe2_5jX5LlLUQOfrWljjKvRhlJy0xHyUuDBDEiHTjyJw3eXNwZyvDyZ1IihudN2XeqR052H9b-Y2zIvqDIZXp6vIvAni4AbwqbLmoecyJ8KPSsmcrum9xZbfwRI1itClxfpangk_uIzCx9O41lbq-ycKSDeUHK3H4b_lJGCYtJD9YVyRseCSP84PJA0CD0IGZ1fG29O8l7RVVfoqRBZ1ih1ANTkzp0J5WQYPjfWpUhj3V2nfknPSh1nv8C2DdHO6GEhhRgiHFACuHOxQoVwXZz872SbMzpFBoR9cBhEsuJjMNMnaa2SZ5L3gSD0LcpwEJBEwvuhXR9SsJJ2M7PCEQQ/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h18/h001.qPsSjzU230CSY6LIWRFVDGL_uJlkpSXvCsJNSZ3vUQI&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;PowerUserAccess vs. AdministratorAccess from an attacker&amp;#39;s perspective&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;OffensAI[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565Sh-SDvgyu6m58HhCZ9db8DGIfJsTOGlv-OfESNH6tS1QQmfqJ1vtG6nuD-AoI7CUsU3Rsq0TTrTet6F21wSAg12mpKhnPVQboe4uv64kZi8CfqV2oOKZs0fbKRg8Gh36_oM3sxCMOhWLr4P7lBycQ0jpFKj_VkPww5wGOOpIE5x3w7_RmI78RDjGGaMCQFVmjpaERoKip8HXF2HR5ApsWw3KerlWHxCN7wZfdpWbE0xSWbkvU5Sw4O7E5cBEVBxlzZzwkBamRqkiSCBaX_C8qRO3iiEgATPRCggkuwAcO51ijuWfOBSUbrIQWlB1hf7uHUJk6LtzvDVjzzOGT2M141Ew/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h19/h001.3noiKiD8EDW-Hf243Ux_Lcojp1NZ0oTI1sGXNVp-TFI&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Eduard Agavriloae&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; describes how the AWS managed policy &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;PowerUserAccess&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; can be as dangerous as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;AdministratorAccess&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; in complex AWS environments. For example, through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;PowerUserAccess&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;, attackers can escalate privileges by modifying and invoking a Lambda function with inappropriate IAM permissions, using SSM SendCommand to exfiltrate access credentials from an EC2 instance with an overly permissive role, or altering a CloudFormation template with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;AdministratorAccess&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; to include a privilege escalation vector.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.jDp7yZmWUrSClxco9LCz79B9PgAAGPebHE68moM9b12ZfgHluRTs5ohmHLMJNYH2xmH36zcHFCUK0Qj2CpEMB9gM4HLljBK8NYSxkJceqraB1GRKSsp6wPIPt86ZZOYE5sfpUPAIzaZVFzMZRKlNboUB8Mi79yK_c67YmHQVry8QIhZ-XbebD5wLADYfiXkIHdFpK0AsHaVgKNETga5SzMYysNanrRMrfOmpYWRGb6W8_rCG2VoFxB5-5P_vaj0qPGrEjQE49AYrHw4lQe5WUooKZSr3JZNXMgno_rui5MlcWWaGQgxVqSk2Iq6uwpyq2giYLIgv_9E7-HyDHqfqzg/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h20/h001.Ldvzt2hl3z_hnvcMIGxOK0qq1esgBbF9fBcRDABRA_k&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;State of [0xe2][0x80][0x98]State of Cloud Security[0xe2][0x80][0x99] Reports: Insights or Self-Owns?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565Sh-SDvgyu6m58HhCZ9db8DGKgzARscUAp7kjf9oojOF4o1bATUJx71NsS-PlY-ugCSAyRK6TUFY_C-q26GO_9IJCODLvgqf1qN7-rHOZ4Xj_RpGt9PXOfoR0KtCit7fDJ3W8nQYDCteCDnHopGPSIqiPN7CoH_8B0Sbv-qm2VzUYVwrzLqMt-If43evlkS3oyCBsEotpcdjBOk1Vu6dSayrAABIKQKJHMK07VEx99yB8U4vqUmXZNqPTfefNXIXjoktnDdcHEzRsn9qVwia3SO4_4yRoTO9UAigO9QjTZfrdxeyPfT6iFUi6gPzlaMZSKxg/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h21/h001.UpQsA76TmxRCaWd1lI3Bee8bFPoHH-MHpsUajgM4RZM&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Rami McCarthy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; takes a critical look at &amp;quot;state of cloud security&amp;quot; reports published by CSPM vendors, highlighting how these reports may reflect more on the product&amp;#39;s effectiveness than the actual state of cloud security, and how certain stats might not represent real security risk or there may be a legit reason for the observed state. [0xe2][0x80][0x9c]Often, the statistics presented are as much a reflection of limitation in collected or analyzed data, or the product, as any specific research perspective.[0xe2][0x80][0x9d]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt; [0xf0][0x9f][0x92][0xa1]&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; I like this angle, and in general I think as an industry we should do a better job at critically analyzing [0xe2][0x80][0x9c]state of the union[0xe2][0x80][0x9d] type reports, evaluations/benchmarks, etc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565ShwPFeE2dDyO14Xqz8fR5FCCCmKojDhVXTKDXLz6dxsXb3WGk455S2y9poTciWH8JmbUGxRrFuB_FZwnuiAl_Ghvtu3qNXPXDrsCBXAPwLuTlI_JvRHC3No6LL_x4ePJkdEcxv0g2QjOAkKzEiBnoXnpY1H1eUKyBtLisNmD5SUy5xuKFN_lgax1E3kELorROsTWRTnQh02g6pubsFnmaJTicnMosHpg1Mn-ndME49p9BvojlUljIHFUfH-hyANquztDCoTYRbgHzGzr7sDOD3xOTrIJWTi5LS90JJch1ecF2qX95bQbk0Lc6yN4LkYHf1B2LNHpalyZq5Ku2J8dyQVUZD5QF0XnwoCAYrT0pjqBpg4pGL2rkn_1WAC_syDwMgQ/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h22/h001.MCG54DJXpsE7D3dnmn5ksnDcnEBfOE-GDGXVRN1tSEc&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Beyond Configuration Perfection: Redefining [0xe2][0x80][0x98]Cloud Security[0xe2][0x80][0x99]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Vectra AI[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.-QQnKmN9995ElcpR565Sh-SDvgyu6m58HhCZ9db8DGKIKnHg35KBbVrDXhgzlXBdX5mLOlXUfyyDZ6uO5EPC4o90G2_DKuVZG9XsC47rgpdBohYZ1p3CrcIOtXaQLt3GMg0Lv6KndUn_jMoSgyOJKCwpBljeDabGsb5naqhCOga3spkP8ZLeH4NFpqNIS_6lYZJ_y4hueBBPUCXK02DvD_Py2rpUwVlM2VG-XCfEYXlfH814SUWGsrX-6JW9Djsmyk7WH9Cby8wsQCFbdNfj4BB4Qz3W"
[2025-04-14 21:29:26,329][DEBUG][org.apache.http.wire] http-outgoing-20 << "SKBGbAGDidb2yqxyrjBwabHIsqsfp0uaO4V91MqytJluMQEJeyyDLwuSX4HuYad2xGbb2FvP_sV65BM/4f5/Bfq3makRTpKF0Npi0qUnIA/h23/h001.seqiuwUpB_kCcPG0mk9XOT83Sps5c288YX25xq3Wq1A&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Kat Traxler&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt; argues that focusing on cloud misconfigurations and least-privilege access alone can cause security teams to underinvest in other important areas, like threat detection and incident response, security automation and orchestration, and governance and risk management. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;She also makes good points about the potentially questionable reliability of industry reports and metrics (e.g. X% of orgs have &amp;lt;something risky&amp;gt;), because a) this is based on one vendor[0xe2][0x80][0x99]s customers (which may not be representative of all companies), and b) the sample size/which customers are included may vary from year to year, so stats might naturally fluctuate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table role=&quot;none&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td bgcolor=&quot;transparent&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent;padding:0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;table role=&quot;none&quot; widt