to carve strings out of remote process memory. This tool allows operators to carve ASCII and UTF-16 strings from targeted processes, making it effective for retrieving JWT tokens, credentials, and other sensitive data directly from memory.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&quot;dd&quot; align=&quot;left&quot; style=&quot;padding:0px 15px;text-align:left;word-break:break-word;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height:24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;link&quot; href=&quot;https://link.mail.beehiiv.com/ss/c/u001.m5CTo68rhNghfieTCcZktvzLXzATDwVqXkGyJ7Ijf2km6-y1EvKbnQilZ_qRed0q6ELnCUaKExwZNG05Mo42WpvgpGvOil5QCcSJFTpQT1J6KWfeRlXnkN7lCye6oulIk_U8ge8bvwHBBy3oF8wPkRUclpzslqirH5vKsZorxKb0PICKV8RxvYdHTT-guvO7JYPCTsu4oPS58RAH7TUiW6YpoZtxIXLlNF8x5zG-CZhWV-5pXUUu64WbBobcA9iE-9zsxDivCAGvBp_0WZQ6eZhOPoQOfBZT6mmY-y0AP8P5iRuckKrn5_KiHgsnRz-I/4er/A_O0QUTdQvKpB6LLxIdwkg/h42/h001.7fp3dCtzSMeh7mi8XVthzklDiYRw6DHi2hGcuusLPaM&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer nofollow&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;hardenedlinux/userland-exec&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Userland exec replaces the existing process image within the current address space with a new one. It mimics the behavior of the system call &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;execve&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;, but the process structures describing the process image remain unchanged (the process name reported by system utilities will retain the old process name). This can be used to achieve stealth after gaining arbitrary code execution as well as to execute binaries stored in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;noexec&lt;/code&gt;&l